+  <para>
+   Advice is applied to every query planned while it is in force, and
+   different queries can use the same alias for different tables; for
+   example, the queries <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> runs to check
+   foreign keys all alias their table <literal>x</literal>. An advice target
+   can therefore name the relation that its alias must refer to:
+  </para>
+
+<programlisting>
+alias_name#occurrence_number:schema.relation/partition_schema.partition_name@plan_name
+</programlisting>
+
+  <para>
+   Such a target matches what the same target without
+   <literal>:schema.relation</literal> would match, but only if the alias
+   refers to that relation, which must be schema-qualified; for a partition,
+   it is the partitioned table that the alias refers to. For example,
+   <literal>INDEX_SCAN(x:public.orders public.orders_pkey)</literal> applies
+   to a query whose alias <literal>x</literal> refers to
+   <literal>public.orders</literal>, and to no other query. Generated advice
+   does not include the relation, since it is not needed to identify a
+   relation within the query the advice was generated from.
+  </para>
+
